# LightGlue's native integration forwarded the config object's own
# trust_remote_code flag into the HuggingFace auto-class loaders. The flag is
# documented as the caller's explicit trust decision -- when it is True,
# AutoConfig.from_pretrained / AutoModel*.from_config download the model
# repository's own Python files and execute them -- but the config object is
# itself built from the repository's config.json, so a malicious repository
# sets "trust_remote_code": true and its code runs without the caller opting
# in (CWE-829, CWE-94). The fixed revision drops the keyword from both call sites and the
# codegen source; the loaders stay, only the artifact-supplied opt-in goes.
#
# The weakness class is new vocabulary: code.LoadedDataControlsCodeExecutionOptIn
# (VYQL-INJ-277) covers any loader whose code-execution opt-in is read back
# from the object being loaded. The Python binding
# (bindings/python/remote_code_opt_in_from_loaded_data.vyql) is written from
# the loaders' own documentation and discriminates on the argument text: the
# caller's-choice spellings measured in the same checkout -- the auto-class API
# forwarding its own trust_remote_code parameter, an explicit
# trust_remote_code=True literal in conversion tooling, and the argparse
# args./model_args./data_args.trust_remote_code the example scripts read from
# the operator's command line (24 findings on examples/pytorch/language-
# modeling before that decline, 0 after) -- never read the flag from an
# attribute of the artifact, so none carries the ".trust_remote_code" argument
# text the binding requires. The one residual, stated in the binding:
# transformers' CLI server stores the operator's --trust_remote-code option as
# self.trust_remote_code, textually identical to a config class reading its
# own field, so its two loader calls still read through.

test "a loader whose remote-code opt-in is read from the loaded config"
  lang python
  profile library
  expect VYQL-INJ-277
  expect_review code.LoadedDataControlsCodeExecutionOptIn
  file src/transformers/models/lightglue/configuration_lightglue.py
  code
  ```
  from transformers import AutoConfig
  from transformers.models.auto.auto_factory import CONFIG_MAPPING


  class LightGlueConfig:
      trust_remote_code: bool = False

      def __post_init__(self, **kwargs):
          if isinstance(self.keypoint_detector_config, dict):
              self.keypoint_detector_config["model_type"] = self.keypoint_detector_config.get("model_type", "superpoint")
              if self.keypoint_detector_config["model_type"] not in CONFIG_MAPPING:
                  self.keypoint_detector_config = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(
                      self.keypoint_detector_config["_name_or_path"], trust_remote_code=self.trust_remote_code
                  )
  ```

test "a detector construction taking the opt-in from the config object"
  lang python
  profile library
  expect VYQL-INJ-277
  expect_review code.LoadedDataControlsCodeExecutionOptIn
  file src/transformers/models/lightglue/modeling_lightglue.py
  code
  ```
  from transformers import AutoModelForKeypointDetection


  class LightGlueForKeypointMatching:
      def __init__(self, config):
          super().__init__(config)
          self.keypoint_detector = AutoModelForKeypointDetection.from_config(
              config.keypoint_detector_config, trust_remote_code=config.trust_remote_code
          )
  ```

test "the patched form loads through the registry without the opt-in"
  lang python
  profile library
  reject VYQL-INJ-277
  reject_review code.LoadedDataControlsCodeExecutionOptIn
  file src/transformers/models/lightglue/configuration_lightglue.py
  code
  ```
  from transformers.models.auto.auto_factory import CONFIG_MAPPING


  class LightGlueConfig:
      def __post_init__(self, **kwargs):
          if isinstance(self.keypoint_detector_config, dict):
              self.keypoint_detector_config["model_type"] = self.keypoint_detector_config.get("model_type", "superpoint")
              self.keypoint_detector_config = CONFIG_MAPPING[self.keypoint_detector_config["model_type"]](
                  **self.keypoint_detector_config, attn_implementation="eager"
              )
  ```

